Пример использования `getContent()`, отправка RawData from javascript

The `getContent()` method in Laravel is used to retrieve the raw content of the HTTP request. It is commonly used to access the content of the request body, especially when dealing with requests that contain data in formats like JSON or XML. The method allows developers to extract and process the raw content of the request for further manipulation or validation within the Laravel application.

&lt;div class=&quot;prose dark:prose-invert inline leading-normal break-words min-w-0 [word-break:break-word]&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;&quot;&gt;To send data from JavaScript, specifically with a demo object, to the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;getContent()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;&quot;&gt; method in Laravel, you can achieve this by making an HTTP POST request from your JavaScript code to a Laravel route that handles the request. Here&#039;s a general outline of how you can accomplish this:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;ol class=&quot;list-outside list-decimal marker:font-mono marker:text-sm pl-11&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;&quot;&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;JavaScript Code (Client-Side):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;&quot;&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;ul class=&quot;list-outside list-disc&quot;&gt;
